A datatype-rank comparison no longer counts as a finite bound for finite
set or map comprehensions. A datatype containing an infinite set can have
infinitely many values below its rank. Use a genuinely finite bound, such
as membership in a finite collection, or an infinite comprehension instead.

Finite-domain map types no longer count as finite carriers when their value
types are infinite. Comprehensions using those complete map values as set
elements or map keys need a finite witness bound. Maps with finite key
carriers still admit arbitrary value types.
